AI Engineer

Job Title: AI Engineer / Machine Learning Engineer
Experience: 2–5 Years
Employment Type: Full-Time

Job Description

We are looking for an AI Engineer to design, develop, and deploy AI/ML-powered applications. The ideal candidate should have strong Python and machine learning fundamentals, along with practical experience working with LLMs, RAG systems, NLP, or predictive models.

Responsibilities
Design and develop AI/ML solutions for real-world business problems.
Build, evaluate, and deploy machine learning models.
Develop applications using Large Language Models (LLMs).
Build RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipelines.
Implement document processing, chunking, embeddings, and vector search.
Work with vector databases and semantic search.
Integrate models through APIs and AI platforms.
Develop prompt engineering and evaluation strategies.
Fine-tune or adapt models when required.
Build AI agents and tool-using workflows where appropriate.
Evaluate model quality, accuracy, latency, and cost.
Implement monitoring and feedback mechanisms for AI applications.
Collaborate with backend, data, and product teams.
Required Skills
Strong Python programming skills.
Understanding of Machine Learning and AI fundamentals.
Experience with LLMs and Generative AI.
Knowledge of Prompt Engineering.
Hands-on experience with RAG.
Understanding of embeddings and vector databases.
Experience with APIs and backend application development.
Knowledge of NLP concepts.
Familiarity with frameworks such as LangChain, LlamaIndex, or similar.
Experience with models/APIs from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, open-source models, or equivalent.
Understanding of model evaluation and AI application reliability.
Preferred Skills
PyTorch or TensorFlow.
Hugging Face.
FAISS, Pinecone, Weaviate, Milvus, or pgvector.
Agentic AI.
Fine-tuning and LoRA/PEFT.
MLflow.
Docker and Kubernetes.
AWS/Azure/GCP AI/ML services.